{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 521198, "name": "Ruslan Bekenev", "username": "krydos", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/krydos/{size}/33136_2.png", "created_at": "2026-08-03T10:24:44.221Z", "cooked": "<p>Hi everyone,</p>\n<p>I went to bugzilla hoping to pick up an orphan package that I’d like to support but filtering by Orphan Owner (all opened statuses) I found lots of tickets for packages that are long time retired [1], [2].</p>\n<p>I imagine it’s maybe not the right approach of picking up an orphaned package but now I’m curious. Is it intentional that we keep these tickets opened in bugzilla? What is the purpose of these opened tickets?</p>\n<p>[1] <a href=\"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1116840\" class=\"inline-onebox\">1116840 – drwright-3.5.0 is available</a></p>\n<p>[2] <a href=\"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1136298\" class=\"inline-onebox\">1136298 – tcpcopy-1.0.0 is available</a></p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2026-08-03T13:21:50.648Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 10, "reads": 45, "readers_count": 44, "score": 79.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 198327, "topic_slug": "help-me-understand-orphan-owner-in-bugzilla", "display_username": "Ruslan Bekenev", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1116840", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "1116840 – drwright-3.5.0 is available", "clicks": 5}, {"url": "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1136298", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "1136298 – tcpcopy-1.0.0 is available", "clicks": 3}], "read": true, "user_title": "Packaging Team", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 18012, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/help-me-understand-orphan-owner-in-bugzilla/198327/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 521234, "name": "FranciscoD", "username": "ankursinha", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/ankursinha/{size}/71_2.png", "created_at": "2026-08-03T13:21:33.710Z", "cooked": "<p>I believe the idea is that if someone takes over the package, the bugs get assigned to them. Closing tickets will mean that new maintainers will not be aware of open/existing bugs against packages.</p>\n<p>Picking up orphaned packages is done on <a href=\"https://src.fedoraproject.org\">https://src.fedoraproject.org</a>. When we take over orphaned packages there, the bugzilla asignee etc. are automatically updated in a bit.</p>\n<aside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://docs.fedoraproject.org/en-US/package-maintainers/Package_Orphaning_Process/#claiming_ownership_of_an_orphaned_package\">\n  <header class=\"source\">\n\n      <a href=\"https://docs.fedoraproject.org/en-US/package-maintainers/Package_Orphaning_Process/#claiming_ownership_of_an_orphaned_package\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Fedora Docs</a>\n  </header>\n\n  <article class=\"onebox-body\">\n    <div class=\"aspect-image\" style=\"--aspect-ratio:225/62;\"><img src=\"https://docs.fedoraproject.org/en-US/_/img/docs_logo.png\" class=\"thumbnail\" alt=\"\" width=\"225\" height=\"62\"></div>\n\n<h3><a href=\"https://docs.fedoraproject.org/en-US/package-maintainers/Package_Orphaning_Process/#claiming_ownership_of_an_orphaned_package\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claiming Ownership of an Orphaned Package - Package Orphaning Process</a></h3>\n\n  <p>This page contains instructions for working with orphan packages as specified in Policy for Orphan and Retired Packages. | Learn more about Fedora Linux, the Fedora Project &amp; the Fedora Community.</p>\n\n\n  </article>\n\n  <div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n    \n    \n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2026-08-03T13:21:33.710Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 40, "readers_count": 39, "score": 28.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 198327, "topic_slug": "help-me-understand-orphan-owner-in-bugzilla", "display_username": "FranciscoD", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://docs.fedoraproject.org/en-US/package-maintainers/Package_Orphaning_Process/#claiming_ownership_of_an_orphaned_package", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Making sure you're not a bot!", "clicks": 1}, {"url": "https://src.fedoraproject.org", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Making sure you're not a bot!", "clicks": 0}], "read": true, "user_title": "", "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": true, "admin": false, "staff": true, "user_id": 78, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/help-me-understand-orphan-owner-in-bugzilla/198327/2", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 521404, "name": "Ruslan Bekenev", "username": "krydos", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/krydos/{size}/33136_2.png", "created_at": "2026-08-04T09:14:31.387Z", "cooked": "<p>I think it makes sense with orphan packages, I agree. Two packages that I mentioned are <strong>retired</strong> actually and I think this is what makes me confused. I guess your logic is applicable for retired packages as well. If I decide to unretire a package I better know what were the known bugs before it was retired.</p>\n<p>But doesn’t mean that bugs for retired packages will never be closed?</p>", "post_number": 5, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2026-08-04T09:14:31.387Z", "reply_count": 2, "reply_to_post_number": 2, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 1, "reads": 35, "readers_count": 34, "score": 37.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 198327, "topic_slug": "help-me-understand-orphan-owner-in-bugzilla", "display_username": "Ruslan Bekenev", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Packaging Team", "title_is_group": false, "reply_to_user": {"id": 78, "username": "ankursinha", "name": "FranciscoD", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/ankursinha/{size}/71_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 18012, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/help-me-understand-orphan-owner-in-bugzilla/198327/5", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 521406, "name": "FranciscoD", "username": "ankursinha", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/ankursinha/{size}/71_2.png", "created_at": "2026-08-04T09:34:15.592Z", "cooked": "<p>Bugs will be closed by the usual process when a particular Fedora release goes EOL—all bugs filed against that Fedora release are closed. Ones filed against rawhide, though, will remain open forever I expect.</p>", "post_number": 6, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2026-08-04T09:34:15.592Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 5, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 1, "reads": 32, "readers_count": 31, "score": 16.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 198327, "topic_slug": "help-me-understand-orphan-owner-in-bugzilla", "display_username": "FranciscoD", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "reply_to_user": {"id": 18012, "username": "krydos", "name": "Ruslan Bekenev", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/krydos/{size}/33136_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": true, "admin": false, "staff": true, "user_id": 78, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/help-me-understand-orphan-owner-in-bugzilla/198327/6", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 521408, "name": "Ruslan Bekenev", "username": "krydos", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/krydos/{size}/33136_2.png", "created_at": "2026-08-04T09:40:37.344Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"ankursinha\" data-display-name=\"FranciscoD\" data-post=\"6\" data-topic=\"198327\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/ankursinha/48/71_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> FranciscoD:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>all bugs filed against that Fedora release are closed</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Nice! This is good to know.</p>\n<p>Interesting case with rawhide but I don’t have any suggestions here.</p>\n<p>Thank you for the explanations!</p>", "post_number": 7, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2026-08-04T09:40:37.344Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 6, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 33, "readers_count": 32, "score": 21.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 198327, "topic_slug": "help-me-understand-orphan-owner-in-bugzilla", "display_username": "Ruslan Bekenev", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Packaging Team", "title_is_group": false, "reply_to_user": {"id": 78, "username": "ankursinha", "name": "FranciscoD", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/ankursinha/{size}/71_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 18012, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/help-me-understand-orphan-owner-in-bugzilla/198327/7", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 521424, "name": "ilikelinux", "username": "ilikelinux", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/ilikelinux/{size}/27169_2.png", "created_at": "2026-08-04T12:44:43.463Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"krydos\" data-display-name=\"Ruslan Bekenev\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"198327\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/krydos/48/33136_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ruslan Bekenev:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>now I’m curious. Is it intentional that we keep these tickets opened in bugzilla? What is the purpose of these opened tickets?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes I think so that it is intentional. I picked your first app and searched “Upstream”<sup class=\"footnote-ref\"><a href=\"#footnote-521424-1\" id=\"footnote-ref-521424-1\">[1]</a></sup></p>\n<p>Upstream means from where the app came in first place into Fedora:</p><aside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\" data-onebox-src=\"https://wiki.gnome.org/Attic/drwright\">\n  <header class=\"source\">\n\n      <a href=\"https://wiki.gnome.org/Attic/drwright\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">wiki.gnome.org</a>\n  </header>\n\n  <article class=\"onebox-body\">\n    \n\n<h3><a href=\"https://wiki.gnome.org/Attic/drwright\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Attic/drwright – GNOME Wiki Archive</a></h3>\n\n\n\n  </article>\n\n  <div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n    \n    \n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n<p>\nAs you can see, also Gnome retired it, and their link into their Bugzilla is broken. For you as a possible new maintainer not really use full because you wanted to know why in first place the app is not maintained anymore. Till know I just repeated what <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/ankursinha\">@ankursinha</a> said in one sentence.</p>\n<hr>\nAs this app goes back to gnome2, maintainers not had joy, time and probably power to bring the app up to GTK4 and in future to GTK5. Another hurdle is to bring such old apps from x11 to Wayland.\n<p>Now some historical information about Bugzilla. As you can see Bugzilla is still a subdomain of Red Hat. This is because they shared the Bug-tracker with us in the past. They moved on to a “git based” or newer system which suits better for them.</p>\n<p>Fedora recently changed also to the new forge.fp.o to retire “Pagure . io”. This way we probably will be more compatible with other Upstream projects and can just fork their information and add the Fedora part into it.</p>\n <hr>\nAbout alternatives to such old apps you are talking about, there was/is a section in the Magazine where they introduced frequently flatpak apps which covered similar functions. I believe I saw there an app which might is something you could have a look into it.\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"krydos\" data-display-name=\"Ruslan Bekenev\" data-post=\"5\" data-topic=\"198327\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/krydos/48/33136_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ruslan Bekenev:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>But doesn’t mean that bugs for retired packages will never be closed?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I think in your case it was good that the ticked has been filed against rawhide, to get the necessary information while you searched for open tickets <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twemoji/wink.png?v=15\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> If you like, you cloud add the upstream link, and mention that retirement not always happens in Fedora, it also can happen upstream. When people are missing to support or finance this projects, then this happens. And will happen even more in the near future.</p>\n<hr class=\"footnotes-sep\">\n\n<ol class=\"footnotes-list\">\n<li id=\"footnote-521424-1\" class=\"footnote-item\"><p>Please forgive me if it sounds to obvious what I do write here. I try to give insights that also a newer user can follow, and learn to understand, why we do it so. <a href=\"#footnote-ref-521424-1\" class=\"footnote-backref\">↩︎</a></p>\n</li>\n</ol>", "post_number": 8, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2026-08-04T12:46:45.949Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 2, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 30, "readers_count": 29, "score": 21.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 198327, "topic_slug": "help-me-understand-orphan-owner-in-bugzilla", "display_username": "ilikelinux", "primary_group_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": "", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 53, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://wiki.gnome.org/Attic/drwright", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Attic/drwright – GNOME Wiki Archive", "clicks": 0}], "read": true, "user_title": "Let's have a party (Fedora 44)", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 2081, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [{"id": 78, "username": "ankursinha", "name": "FranciscoD", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/ankursinha/{size}/71_2.png"}], "post_url": "/t/help-me-understand-orphan-owner-in-bugzilla/198327/8", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 521462, "name": "Maxwell G", "username": "gotmax23", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/g/294172/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-08-04T16:30:19.345Z", "cooked": "<p>If you want to find orphaned packages that are available to pick up, you can take a look at the orphaned packages report: <a href=\"https://a.gtmx.me/orphans/orphans.txt\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://a.gtmx.me/orphans/orphans.txt</a>. This provides a list of all orphaned packages that have <em>not</em> yet been retired. I send a copy of the report to the devel-announce mailing list every other week, and the web version gets updated every hour or so. Packages that are orphaned without being claimed for &gt;= 6 weeks are automatically retired and then all of the open rawhide bugs are closed.</p>\n<p>If packages are retired for other reasons, it’s possible the people retiring them do not also close all the bugs, but this should eventually happen automatically when the corresponding Fedora release goes EOL, even if the bugs are against rawhide (unless they are against rawhide <em>and</em> have the FutureFeature keyword).</p>", "post_number": 9, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2026-08-04T16:30:19.345Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 1, "reads": 24, "readers_count": 23, "score": 54.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 198327, "topic_slug": "help-me-understand-orphan-owner-in-bugzilla", "display_username": "Maxwell G", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": "fesco", "flair_url": "https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/original/3X/a/f/af3a1ba1ca92e6d3195851ee9e6829a8a2e00586.png", "flair_bg_color": "", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 64, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://a.gtmx.me/orphans/orphans.txt", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "clicks": 2}], "read": true, "user_title": "Fedora Engineering Steering Committee", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 3}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 2562, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/help-me-understand-orphan-owner-in-bugzilla/198327/9", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 3}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 3, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 521523, "name": "Ruslan Bekenev", "username": "krydos", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/krydos/{size}/33136_2.png", "created_at": "2026-08-04T22:36:55.536Z", "cooked": "<p>Ah, beautiful! Thanks guys.</p>\n<p>Both of those tickets I mentioned above do have <code>Futur